Subject: Cantor M2B Post Supplied Root Topology Projection Architecture Review

Description: Between-slice review after all three supplied entry carriers are proven. It selects one lineage-preserving, zero-effect mixed topology inventory assembly while separating supplied-set coherence from physical enumeration, completeness, traversal, digest, receipt, and admission.

@ [topology_forms] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Machine_Forms.sop
@ [scanner_formation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner.sop
@ [root_projection] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_M2B_Supplied_Root_Topology_Projection.sop
@ [directory_projection] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_M2B_Supplied_Directory_Topology_Projection.sop
@ [regular_file_projection] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_M2B_Supplied_Regular_File_Topology_Projection.sop
@ [root_proof] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_M2B_Supplied_Root_Topology_Projection_Proof.sop

& [ReviewIdentity] is exact
  + [review_uuid] is 5c747ef8-6211-4955-ae58-1d1e9845cc25
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [baseline_commit] is 61cfdbf1c007f6b3fd03511112a7722067ffff7b
  + [status] is checkpoint_complete_next_pure_boundary_selected

& [ClosedSupport] is exact
  + one output-only root carrier preserves complete preflight and revalidated directory-stability lineage beside a fixed current-M2A-valid RootDirectory observation
  + output-only descendant-directory and regular-file carriers preserve revalidated lower lineage beside current-M2A-valid observations
  + none of the three carrier types derives Deserialize, exposes public fields, or permits direct construction of successful projection state
  + all three carriers remain supplied structural projections without runtime, physical, enumeration, traversal, inventory, receipt, or admission authority

& [SupportDelta] now exposes set coherence
  + [closed] one root, descendant directory, and regular-file carrier vocabulary
  + [still_open] heterogeneous set assembly with bounded limits
  + [still_open] duplicate projection identity, entry reference, strong identity, and relative-path rejection
  + [still_open] root-first contiguous ordinal accounting and deterministic component-aware path order
  + [still_open] ancestor-directory closure, per-entry limits, entry count, and total file-byte accounting
  + [still_open] canonical byte encoding and aggregate digest
  + [still_open] physical producer, enumeration completeness, traversal provenance, Git reconciliation, double inventory, receipt, and admission

& [CandidateComparison] is dependency ordered
  + [candidate_A] physical scanner or fixture
    - rejected because platform enumeration, handle ownership, traversal, and authorized physical execution remain unsigned
  + [candidate_B] topology receipt or aggregate digest now
    - rejected because no canonical heterogeneous inventory or canonical byte encoding yet exists and quiescent double-inventory evidence is absent
  + [candidate_C] accept raw TopologyEntryObservation values
    - rejected because it would discard the nonforgeable carrier lineage just completed and accept public deserializable forms as projection success
  + [candidate_D] supplied mixed topology inventory assembly
    + consumes exactly one root wrapper plus bounded directory and regular-file wrapper vectors
    + retains each complete carrier inside one ordered output-only member sequence
    + reapplies current M2A validation to every projected observation
    + checks exact set identities, limits, parent closure, ordinals, and deterministic structural order
    + computes only entry count and total regular-file bytes
    + produces no digest, receipt, consistency class, physical claim, or effect

& [SelectedBoundary] is supplied topology inventory assembly
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-topology-inventory-assembly/0.1
  + [target_module] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_supplied_topology_inventory_assembly.rs
  + [plan] strict profile, nonzero assembly identity, and complete TopologyScanLimits under a 16384-byte predecode cap
  + [inputs] one WindowsSuppliedRootTopologyProjection, zero or more WindowsSuppliedDirectoryTopologyProjection values, and zero or more WindowsSuppliedRegularFileTopologyProjection values
  + [carrier_rule] no raw observation, preflight fragment, stable pair, digest binding, or projection success fragment is accepted
  + [revalidation] current ValidateTopologyForm runs on limits and every carrier observation
  + [cardinality] root is exactly one by function shape; total entries are nonzero, safely countable as u64, and within maximum_entries
  + [volume] every entry StrongFileIdentity volume_serial equals the root value exactly
  + [uniqueness] nonzero projection identities, nonzero entry-reference identities, complete strong identities, descendant paths, and observation ordinals are each unique
  + [shape] root remains RootDirectory with None path and ordinal one; every other member remains Directory or RegularFile with Some path
  + [limits] path UTF-8 bytes, component depth, stream count, per-file bytes, and checked aggregate file bytes remain within supplied valid limits
  + [parent_closure] every non-top-level descendant has each proper prefix represented exactly once as Directory
  + [order] component-aware raw UTF-8 byte order compares path components lexicographically and places a parent before its descendant
  + [ordinal] canonical descendant position plus two equals the existing observation ordinal exactly; no sort rewrites a carrier ordinal
  + [accounting] output entry_count and total_file_bytes are derived with checked arithmetic
  + [output] private Serialize-only wrapper retains plan and one ordered enum whose variants own the complete root, directory, or regular-file carrier

& [CanonicalOrderBoundary] is structural and narrow
  + validated relative paths are split only on their existing forward-slash separator
  + components compare by exact raw UTF-8 byte sequence
  + equal shared prefixes place the shorter component sequence first
  + kind is never used as an order tiebreaker because duplicate relative paths reject first
  + ordinal must already equal this order and is not repaired or renumbered
  - never: call this physical traversal order, filesystem collation, case-insensitive Windows order, Git tree order, Unicode-normalized order, or proof of enumeration sequence

& [LimitBoundary] is supplied policy correlation only
  + TopologyScanLimits is public caller syntax and current validation proves only internal form coherence
  + maximum_depth, maximum_path_bytes, maximum_streams_per_entry, maximum_file_bytes, maximum_total_bytes, and maximum_entries are applied structurally
  + deadline_tick is retained but no clock is read and no freshness or completion-before-deadline claim is made
  + allocation already performed by the caller is not retroactively bounded; the assembly checks cardinality before internal ordered-member growth

& [LineageBoundary] is capability-like but not physical
  + carrier wrappers can be obtained through current successful pure projection calls and cannot be deserialized
  + the assembly preserves rather than reconstructs or downgrades those wrappers
  + current M2A observation rules are reapplied at the composition boundary
  + lower preflight, stability, content-binding, and projection evaluations are not falsely described as rerun by the assembly
  - never: infer that in-process nonforgeability proves the supplied lower records originated from Windows, one root, one handle, or one actual traversal

& [EvidenceGrade] is supplied structurally closed set
  + [supplied] limits and all lower records originally supplied to carrier constructors
  + [projected] three nonforgeable carrier families
  + [revalidated] current M2A entry and limit validators only at this boundary
  + [set_correlated] exact volume, identity, reference, path, ordinal, order, ancestor, and limit relationships within the supplied member set
  + [physical_enumerated_complete_traversed_double_checked_digest_bound_receipted_admitted] absent

& [RequirementDelta] is proposed M2B-SSTIA-001 through M2B-SSTIA-016
  + [authority_state] unprocessed_source_not_yet_preserved
  + [effect_state] zero

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  - no filesystem, Windows call, handle, pointer, unsafe, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, Git command, fixture, traversal, physical inventory, digest commitment, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, or promotion
  - stop on any request to treat supplied-set closure as physical inventory completeness
  - stop on any canonical encoding or digest design hidden inside implementation rather than separately specified

& [Decision] is continue only through source preservation and governing SJS before implementation
  + [next] preserve the selected boundary byte-exactly as a new raw source document
  + [then] run full SJS explosion, constraints, data design, justification, plan, registry, matrix, slice, and satisfaction signature
  + [implementation_authority] absent until that signature exists
